{
  "profile": "october-main-text-v1",
  "rulebook": "rulebook/october-main-text-v1.md",
  "reading": "Every number is a decimal string of an exact integer. Each case has exactly four keys: id, kind, inputs and expected. The parameters and a case's inputs are everything needed to compute it; expected holds either exact amounts or one code, or, for a ledger case, the balances after its last step, what each observe step was shown and the code of each refused step. Deleting every case's expected leaves the inputs alone. A claim case names the round case it was earned in, whose inputs it uses. The round of a ceiling, round or claim case is the emission index r; the round of a ledger step is the on-chain round R, counted from 1, with r = R - 1. A ledger case starts from a fresh deployment and its steps run in the order of their step numbers.",
  "units": {
    "usdc": "micro-USDC, 10^-6 USDC",
    "lpt": "wei, 10^-18 LPT",
    "millionths": "the cut, the emission shares and a score are integers over 1000000",
    "rounds": "a ledger step's round is the on-chain round R from 1; ceiling, round and claim cases count the emission index r = R - 1"
